OL,3,GNEWSAUK falls silent to mark Armistice
OL,4,ADay
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe UK has fallen silent to mark
OL,7,FArmistice Day, commemorating the end of
OL,8,FWorld War One.
OL,10,FThe two-minute silence took place to
OL,11,Fmark the end of the war and to remember
OL,12,Fthose who have died in conflicts.
OL,14,FDefence Secretary Wes Streeting laid a
OL,15,Fwreath at the Cenotaph memorial in
OL,16,FLondon, which was also attended by
OL,17,Fsenior military figures, schoolchildren
OL,18,Fand cadets.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
